+# Windows store correction 1/2 summary
+
+Gated Unix-only storage imports and helpers in `lib.rs`. Added three Windows-only tests that use isolated, unique Credential Manager targets with the real WinCred adapter, shared storage engine, and reviewed mutex. Test cleanup deletes only targets written by that test. Production's fixed primary/candidate names are unchanged.
+
+Linux verification passed: 94 library tests, 11 CLI tests and example tests, formatting, Clippy with `-Dwarnings`, and the release build. The isolated real store and lock modules, including native test source, pass Windows-target type checks with `RUSTFLAGS=-Dwarnings`. Native Windows execution is **PENDING**; the test executable could not be linked here because MSVC `link.exe` is unavailable.
+
+Main Windows `--lib` still fails on the known Unix process and signal code. `--all-targets` also reports legacy Unix-only test fixture errors. Exact diagnostics and source commands are in [the evidence log](/home/abdel/Documents/Coding/binus-cli/.agent/windows-store-fix1-evidence.md) and [compiler log](/home/abdel/Documents/Coding/binus-cli/.agent/windows-store-fix1-main-windows.log).
+
+The appended correction in the earlier implementation evidence clarifies that native WinCred operation tests were absent before this pass, the prior main-Windows error attribution was overly broad, and earlier pre-task hashes were not captured (the dirty tree was not an obstacle). This completes only correction 1/2; parent focused review is still required. No browser port, login, API access, real credentials, reboot, commit, or push was performed.
